  "description": "AGSC-05-09 (amended 2026-10-02 for 1.0.0): the WHOLE of graph.jsonld and of each per-item file /pages/<slug>.jsonld, for three items — a concept that requires a second concept and sits in a cluster, the second concept with one source, and the cluster. The dataset is the one the N-Quads lines state (AGSC-05-06). The expected documents are derived by hand from the rule's shape: two members, @context the URL the input names and @graph one node per subject in code-point order of @id; @type the context's term name; each predicate under its term name, an @id-typed term's IRI as a bare string, a language-tagged literal as {@language, @value}, an xsd:string literal or one of the term's own datatype as its bare lexical form; one value bare, never a one-element array. The term names are those of the published context (AGSC-06-32), generated from ontology/agsc.ttl. Each per-item file holds the Bundle node, the item's node and the item's own #source-<n> nodes, identical to their nodes in graph.jsonld: beta's file carries the computed inverse isRequiredBy, and alpha's file carries no cluster membership, because the cluster's skos:member triple has the cluster as its subject. Documents are compared after JCS (AGSC-04-04).",
